PYTHON-LIKE SCRIPT EXAMPLES (noninteractive)

Write to /tmp/demo.py via MCP write_file, then:
  python /tmp/demo.py

1. Arithmetic and iteration
  total = 0
  for i in range(1, 5):
      total = total + i
  print(total)
Expected: 10

2. Inspect a small part of shared memory
  fd = open("/dev/shm", O_RDONLY)
  data = read(fd, 16)
  print(data)
  close(fd)
Read is assigned to a variable; length <=64. Shared memory
contains live bytes; do not modify unless authorized.

3. Send a UDP message to an existing listener
  s = socket(2)
  n = sendto(s, "hello", "127.0.0.1", 2000)
  print(n)
  close(s)
Only run if a service is expected at the destination/port.
This example can have side effects if it targets device-control UDP.
Inspect current services and get approval before sending.

4. Read a few bytes from a virtual file
  f = open("/proc/net/wifi", O_RDONLY)
  b = read(f, 32)
  print(b)
  close(f)
Read from fixed virtual paths may be time-varying.

Do not use import time, socket library, pathlib, file objects,
with/open context managers, def, classes or CPython packages.
For longer scripts split files into smaller tasks rather than
exceeding the 2048-byte source limit.
